ulation 2 + Auspex 1 + Team Assist? = 13","project_3_xp":"n/a","xp_spend":"I didn't spend any yet","lore_request":"how cult and cruac work","vamping":"Hung out with Brandy while patrolling\nChatted with Renee\nVisited family\nPanicked internally about being regent","form_feedback":"google forms ate my response and I couldn't find how to maintain cult or if I should maintain family"},"updated_at":"2026-04-16T20:45:09.369Z","feeding_review":{"pool_player":"Intelligence + Stealth","pool_validated":"Intelligence 4 + Stealth 2 + 4 = 10","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"694104767298797618","author_name":"Angelus","text":"AM Note: Notes target but not method, suggests Wits + Stealth or Dexterity + Stealth.","created_at":"2026-04-12T07:46:48.258Z"}],"story_context":"Expression or Subterfuge would have also been good skills for this method.","pool_mod_equipment":4,"vitae_mod_manual":0,"vitae_rite_cost":1,"nine_again":false,"description":"Hangs out near the Ivy club and feeds on a guy trying to pressure a far too drunk girl to go home with him.","blood_type":"Human","eight_again":false,"pool_validated_by":"Angelus","pool_committed_by":"Angelus"},"projects_resolved":[{"action_type":"patrol_scout","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[8,0>8,8,2,0>2]","successes":5,"exceptional":true,"rolled_at":"2026-04-14T09:42:18.956Z","params":{"size":5,"again":10,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"Presence 3 + Socialise 2 + Contact street 3 = 8","pool_validated":"Presence 3 + Socialise 2 = 5","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"action_type_override":null,"connected_chars":["Brandy LaRoux","Ivana Horvat"],"active_feed_specs":[],"pool_mod_spec":0,"nine_again":false,"rote":false,"eight_again":false,"pool_validated_by":"Angelus"},{"action_type":"hide_protect","pool":null,"roll":null,"st_note":"","pool_player":"placeholder while saving","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"no_roll","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"All your bases r belong to us... but more paranoia and the cult bands together.","created_at":"2026-04-16T09:59:32.764Z"}],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"action_type_override":"maintenance"},{"action_type":"misc","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[3,5,7,9,2,9,6,9]","successes":3,"exceptional":false,"rolled_at":"2026-04-15T05:10:11.401Z","params":{"size":8,"again":10,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"Cruac 1 + Occult 3 + Presence 3 + Expression 3 + Manipulation 2 + Auspex 1 + Team Assist? = 13","pool_validated":"Wits 3 + Occult 3 + Cruac 1 + 1 = 8","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"This supports the Big Crone Ritual \"We Own the Night\"","created_at":"2026-04-14T09:50:14.858Z"}],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"action_type_override":"support","connected_chars":["Anichka","Brandy LaRoux","Cyrus Reynolds","Jack Fallow","Keeper"],"title":"We Own the Night","desired_outcome":"Blush of Life for the night","description":"Ritual Casting a variation of 'Mantle of the Predator Goddess'. \nAs with Mantle of Amorous Fire, Acolytes dance themselves into a trance during the entire casting of this ritual and adopt the Blush of Life. They each must spend a point of Willpower to rise from the exhaustion. Once cast, the Acolytes flow with the grace of a perfect predator for the rest of the night. The Kine all but beg for their attention, stumbling into vulnerable positions with a subconscious prayer to prostrate themselves on her altar. The Acolytes are worshiped as Gods during the Rave. \nThe vibe of this party permeates The Academy.","merits_bonuses":"Mantle of Amrous Fire + Viral Mythology + Cacophony Savvy","active_feed_specs":[],"pool_mod_spec":0,"nine_again":false,"rote":false,"eight_again":false,"pool_mod_equipment":1,"pool_validated_by":"Angelus"}],"st_review":{"territory_overrides":{"0":"northshore","2":"academy","feeding":["northshore"]},"feeding_rote":false,"sighted":{"xp":true},"travel_discretion":"obvious","outcome_text":"## Letter from Home\n\nAlice,\nYou buried the news about your new position three paragraphs into an email about the heating, which is exactly what you did when you got accepted into your programme and exactly what you did when you moved to Sydney in the first place. One day you will lead with the important thing, and I will need to sit down from the shock of it.\nSo you have a position at your club. People are apparently looking to you for something, and you are handling this by being nervous about it in writing to your family instead of telling anyone there that you are nervous about it. I recognise this because I have watched you do it your entire adult life. You collect responsibilities the way other people collect receipts, quietly and without telling anyone, and then you are surprised when the pile gets heavy.\nThe other thing you mentioned, about the people talking about bringing back the old ways, the old guard: I know what that sounds like to you. I know what it does to your shoulders and your jaw. You get that from Dad, who once argued with a man at a petrol station for twenty minutes about something that turned out to be a misunderstanding, and did not apologise afterwards because he said the principle still stood.\nBut you are there now, Alice. You chose to be there. If something needs saying, say it to the people in the room, not to me in an email at two in the morning.\nDad asks if you are eating. I am not going to pass on his exact words because they were mostly about soup.\n\n## Touchstone\n\nYour sister's phone buzzes three times during the walk from the car to the restaurant, and she answers none of them. This is how you know she has been looking forward to seeing you: she has decided, for the duration of the evening, that nobody else exists. She does this rarely and only for people she considers worth the silence, and you have never once taken it for granted.\nShe picks the place, because she always picks the place, and it is a small Vietnamese restaurant on a side street in Marrickville where the menus are laminated and the woman behind the counter remembers her order from last time. Your sister finds this deeply satisfying. She tells you about it twice: once when you sit down and once when the food arrives, as though the continuity of being remembered by a stranger is proof that the world is functioning correctly.\nYou order something you will not eat and move it around the plate with enough conviction that she does not notice. She is telling you about a colleague who has been promoted above his competence, and her analysis of his failings is thorough, specific, and delivered with the calm precision of someone who has been composing this speech in her head for weeks. You ask one question and she talks for another ten minutes, and the relief of being in the presence of someone who requires nothing from you except an audience is so uncomplicated that you almost forget the small rituals: the sip of water, the nod, the laugh at the right moment.\nShe steals a prawn off your plate without asking, which she has done since you were fourteen, and you let her, which you have done for exactly as long.\n\n## The North Shore\n\nThe Shore is at the top of its game and you feel it every way a resident can. Military Road carries confident crowds past eleven. The restaurants in Kirribilli and the bars behind Crows Nest are running late, and foot traffic along the harbour stretches is the healthy kind. Blood comes up clean but the palate catches the faint trace of other feeders having been through ahead of you, nothing wrong with it yet, only a ledger opening. Five of your own are drawing from the territory this month, and three others are feeding here without your grant. Cyrus has been at it without asking. Ivana has been through twice. Wan Yelong is working the lecture crowd with the quiet confidence of somebody who does not think permission applies to him. Past the Oaks on a Tuesday a stranger in the queue behind you is paying closer attention than strangers usually do, and on Willoughby Road you pass through a stretch of pavement that feels listened to.\n\n## Keeping it Tight! (Alice version, credit to Jack)\n\nYou walk the North Shore across four nights, varying your route each time. Brandy takes the harbourside paths with the slow deliberate stride of someone who wants to be noticed, and you cross her circuit twice without needing to coordinate it. Charlie is impossible to track, but notifies you that it is covering the commercial stretches around Military Road with workmanlike efficiency, and you catch the edges of Ivana's movement twice near Cremorne Point.\nThe territory is busy. You count at least six other Kindred feeding here over the course of the month, which is a lot of mouths for one stretch of shoreline. Wan Yelong feeds amongst the harbourside lecture crowd with the quiet confidence of someone who has been doing this for a very long time. Yusuf works the late-night bars with an intensity that leaves a mark on the atmosphere even after he has moved on. One feeder you cannot place at all; you sense the traces of their passage but never see them directly, which tells you something about their methods.\nCyrus you spot twice, feeding in the North Shore without having sought your permission. He is not hiding it.\n\n## Happy Cult\n\nYou spend the month tending the people you have collected. A luncheon at the Mosman house on the second Sunday. A private reading group midweek. Two one-on-one conversations with members who have been anxious about the way the last few weeks have felt, and whose anxiety is useful to register rather than to dismiss. The paranoia is higher this cycle than you remember it being, and the paranoia is the bond. The cult closes around itself. Your base and your people are yours.\n\n## We Own the Night\n\nYour contribution is the oldest trick any of you know. Mantle of Amorous Fire layered into the ritual circle so that everyone who takes up the Cruac's invitation wears the Blush of Life for the night. You lead the portion of the chant that unlocks it. When it takes, a room full of Kindred suddenly breathes, flushes, warms at the skin, is confusable with the mortals on the dance floor below. The dancers who are paying attention take this as a miracle. The ones who are not paying attention take it as the DJ getting the drop right. Either way, the ritual cascades forward.","outcome_visibility":"published","published_at":"2026-04-17T08:16:45.334Z"},"st_narrative":{"feeding_validation":{"approved":true},"letter_from_home":{"response":"Alice,\nYou buried the news about your new position three paragraphs into an email about the heating, which is exactly what you did when you got accepted into your programme and exactly what you did when you moved to Sydney in the first place. One day you will lead with the important thing, and I will need to sit down from the shock of it.\nSo you have a position at your club. People are apparently looking to you for something, and you are handling this by being nervous about it in writing to your family instead of telling anyone there that you are nervous about it. I recognise this because I have watched you do it your entire adult life. You collect responsibilities the way other people collect receipts, quietly and without telling anyone, and then you are surprised when the pile gets heavy.\nThe other thing you mentioned, about the people talking about bringing back the old ways, the old guard: I know what that sounds like to you. I know what it does to your shoulders and your jaw. You get that from Dad, who once argued with a man at a petrol station for twenty minutes about something that turned out to be a misunderstanding, and did not apologise afterwards because he said the principle still stood.\nBut you are there now, Alice. You chose to be there. If something needs saying, say it to the people in the room, not to me in an email at two in the morning.\nDad asks if you are eating. I am not going to pass on his exact words because they were mostly about soup.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete"},"touchstone":{"response":"Your sister's phone buzzes three times during the walk from the car to the restaurant, and she answers none of them. This is how you know she has been looking forward to seeing you: she has decided, for the duration of the evening, that nobody else exists. She does this rarely and only for people she considers worth the silence, and you have never once taken it for granted.\nShe picks the place, because she always picks the place, and it is a small Vietnamese restaurant on a side street in Marrickville where the menus are laminated and the woman behind the counter remembers her order from last time. Your sister finds this deeply satisfying. She tells you about it twice: once when you sit down and once when the food arrives, as though the continuity of being remembered by a stranger is proof that the world is functioning correctly.\nYou order something you will not eat and move it around the plate with enough conviction that she does not notice. She is telling you about a colleague who has been promoted above his competence, and her analysis of his failings is thorough, specific, and delivered with the calm precision of someone who has been composing this speech in her head for weeks. You ask one question and she talks for another ten minutes, and the relief of being in the presence of someone who requires nothing from you except an audience is so uncomplicated that you almost forget the small rituals: the sip of water, the nod, the laugh at the right moment.\nShe steals a prawn off your plate without asking, which she has done since you were fourteen, and you let her, which you have done for exactly as long.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete"},"territory_reports":[{"territory_id":"northshore","response":"The Shore is at the top of its game and you feel it every way a resident can. Military Road carries confident crowds past eleven. The restaurants in Kirribilli and the bars behind Crows Nest are running late, and foot traffic along the harbour stretches is the healthy kind. Blood comes up clean but the palate catches the faint trace of other feeders having been through ahead of you, nothing wrong with it yet, only a ledger opening. Five of your own are drawing from the territory this month, and three others are feeding here without your grant. Cyrus has been at it without asking. Ivana has been through twice. Wan Yelong is working the lecture crowd with the quiet confidence of somebody who does not think permission applies to him. Past the Oaks on a Tuesday a stranger in the queue behind you is paying closer attention than strangers usually do, and on Willoughby Road you pass through a stretch of pavement that feels listened to.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete","revision_note":"Cyrus Reynolds is a poacher, should not be listed as co-resident. \nAM: Resolved"}],"project_responses":[{"project_index":0,"response":"You walk the North Shore across four nights, varying your route each time. Brandy takes the harbourside paths with the slow deliberate stride of someone who wants to be noticed, and you cross her circuit twice without needing to coordinate it. Charlie is impossible to track, but notifies you that it is covering the commercial stretches around Military Road with workmanlike efficiency, and you catch the edges of Ivana's movement twice near Cremorne Point.\nThe territory is busy. You count at least six other Kindred feeding here over the course of the month, which is a lot of mouths for one stretch of shoreline. Wan Yelong feeds amongst the harbourside lecture crowd with the quiet confidence of someone who has been doing this for a very long time. Yusuf works the late-night bars with an intensity that leaves a mark on the atmosphere even after he has moved on. One feeder you cannot place at all; you sense the traces of their passage but never see them directly, which tells you something about their methods.\nCyrus you spot twice, feeding in the North Shore without having sought your permission. He is not hiding it.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":1,"response":"You spend the month tending the people you have collected. A luncheon at the Mosman house on the second Sunday. A private reading group midweek. Two one-on-one conversations with members who have been anxious about the way the last few weeks have felt, and whose anxiety is useful to register rather than to dismiss. The paranoia is higher this cycle than you remember it being, and the paranoia is the bond. The cult closes around itself. Your base and your people are yours.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":2,"response":"Your contribution is the oldest trick any of you know. Mantle of Amorous Fire layered into the ritual circle so that everyone who takes up the Cruac's invitation wears the Blush of Life for the night. You lead the portion of the chant that unlocks it. When it takes, a room full of Kindred suddenly breathes, flushes, warms at the skin, is confusable with the mortals on the dance floor below. The dancers who are paying attention take this as a miracle. The ones who are not paying attention take it as the DJ getting the drop right. Either way, the ritual cascades forward.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete","revision_note":""}],"locked":true},"feeding_vitae_tally":{"herd":5,"ambience":3,"ambience_territory":"North Shore","oath_of_fealty":0,"ghouls":0,"rite_cost":1,"manual":0,"total_bonus":7},"feeding_roll_player":{"cols":[{"r":{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":2,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":2,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":5,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":3,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":6,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":6,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":9,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":7,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":6,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]}],"successes":2,"vessels":2,"safeVitae":4,"methodName":"Other","pool":10,"again":10,"breakdown":"ST confirmed: Intelligence 4 + Stealth 2 + 4 = 10","rolledAt":"2026-04-18T08:28:50.811Z","dramaticFailure":false},"feeding_vitae_allocation":[2,2]},{"_id":"69da37d0cc5483a3c77027a2","chapter_id":"69d0a3c5052b57f6be774e69","character_id":"69d73ea49162ece35897a47d","character_name":"Anichka","player_name":"Katie","status":"submitted","timestamp":"11/04/2026 12:27","attended":true,"_raw":{"submission":{"timestamp":"11/04/2026 12:27","email":"i_live_the_dreame@yahoo.com.au","player_name":"Katie","character_name":"Anichka","attended_last_game":true},"narrative":{"travel_description":"Same as last month, if anyone's gunna jump me then sucks to be me LOL\n\nFrom last downtime-\nShe walks, generally, or uses Obs 1 to get a late bus if she gets the chance. I know walking to and from her territory may take multiple nights, but she travels close to waterways and other places with openings to seek shelter in.","game_recount":"- Sat in a corner a lot and did handicrafts. Now all the Crone present (and Charlie) have ribbons from the hunt. Alice helped, so she'll be in any resonance from them, too.\n- Shook hands with a lot of people, especially some of the newcomers\n- Met the Bishop, that was hilarious\n- Met the Keeper's LS interest, Carver. He's interesting, and only here to learn about the past. A bit like me on that one. Mentioned the old Altar. May wanna touch base about that\n- Talked to Tegan ha ha she was not happy I dreamed about her.\n- Did what pushing I could for Alice to guard the North Shore while Charles wasn't here. I hope she gives him a run for his money on it, I think people like having someone 'innocent' in place there, we just need to make sure she gets good guidance if she stays\n- Guided plotting for next game. Made sure Jack and Cyrus (and to a lesser extent Brandi) were on it. \n- Talked to Cyrus, gave my blessing to be involved in the Hunt memories. Really wish the Keeper had been a bit more chill, he really took Cyrus's absence personally.","standout_rp":"Edna/Arlo, we got about two minutes of tense pleasantries in but I've been waiting for it. Peter/Yusuf, very strong character interactions and plotting. Good fun observing the new player in the bright orange-red suit get into character. Honourable mentions to Archer and Kurtis for solid characters that appealed to Anichka.","ic_correspondence":"To my Sire,\n\nOh, the coven near Lviv! A very good place to remember. Are they still there? I hope they are well. I hope Halyna is well.\n\nSydney is... a tribulation. It is raw, cutting grass. A portion of ground has been cut out, but as always, our kind are hungry, circling, wanting more from a city that does not welcome us. Not yet.\n\nThere is so much to do. We have claimed two of the primary territories for feeding. This means I must walk the spaces to help keep them safe. My Maiden, Alice, has been put in charge of one. If anyone takes advantage of her, I think our Circle will take action. Probably sudden and violent action.\n\nI think there is something in the ocean, making people angry. I dreamed of an opening chest there, and our littlest says she has seen an angry lady there. We will investigate, of course, but I do not know if I should put up a wanted poster saying 'Have You Seen This Lady' or not. Time will tell.\n\nI am starting my garden. I have learned about the plants here, cut my hands on them and scratched my feet. I will make them grow and they will fruit with blood. I have also dreamed of the old temple. We will search there and find answers. But not now. We must walk the borders and let the night know what belongs to us.\n\nI wish you could see our work, but you must stay home. When I come back, Gods willing, I will show you through all I have learned.\n\nI remain in service,\nAnichka","most_trusted_pc":"Charlie, Alice, Ivana, with a hat tip to Jack","actively_harming_pc":"Nope!","aspirations":"Short term- Secure the Academy and the North Shore for the Crone, Host good party,make sure she doesn't get eaten by whoever owns the land where she lives.\nMedium term- Continued stability for the Crone, exploration and potentail restoration of the Old Temple, good Mandragora garden.\nLong term- Safety and Stability of self, family, Crone, and Praxis in that order (the middle two points are close)"},"regency":{"is_regent":false,"territory":null,"residency_grants":[],"total_residency_count":null,"regency_action":null},"feeding":{"method":"I HEAR WE'RE HAVING A PARTY. Anichka is discerning with who she feeds from, looking for targets who haven't been drinking heavily or doing drugs (she'll branch out to 'not doing hard drugs' if finding someone with no drugs proves too hard). If it looks particularly sparse, she'll start using Auspex to try and find someone suitable, but not otherwise. Basically just trying to feed sensibly.","territories":{"The Academy":"Not feeding here","The Harbour":"Not feeding here","The Dockyards":"Not feeding here","The Second City":"Not feeding here","The North Shore":"Not feeding here","The Barrens (No Territory)":"Not feeding here"}},"influence":{"The Academy":0,"The Harbour":0,"The Dockyards":0,"The Second City":0,"The Shore":0},"projects":[{"action_type":"patrol_scout","action_type_raw":"Patrol / Scout","primary_pool":{"expression":"Wits + Stealth + Auspex","size":null},"secondary_pool":{"expression":"Intelligence + Occult + Auspex","size":null},"desired_outcome":"Stabilising/patrolling The Academy, and scouting weird stuff","description":"Project Name: Patrolling the Academy\nCharacters involved: Just Anichka, but tangentially involving anyone else spending actions in the territory\nMerits & Bonuses: \nXP Spend: \n\nGenerally keeping an eye out for activities and flows of traffic, night events, little eddies and currents that other people may have missed. Staying undercover. Also keeping all senses open for any occult weirdness that Jack may have missed","project_name":"Patrolling the Academy","characters":null,"xp_spend":null,"merits":null,"bonuses":null,"detail":"Characters involved: Just Anichka, but tangentially involving anyone else spending actions in the territory\nMerits & Bonuses: \nGenerally keeping an eye out for activities and flows of traffic, night events, little eddies and currents that other people may have missed. Staying undercover. Also keeping all senses open for any occult weirdness that Jack may have missed"},{"action_type":"patrol_scout","action_type_raw":"Patrol / Scout","primary_pool":{"expression":"Wits + Stealth + Auspex","size":null},"secondary_pool":{"expression":"Intelligence + Occult+ Auspex","size":null},"desired_outcome":"Stabilising/patrolling The North Shore, and scouting weird stuff","description":"Project Name: Patrolling the Shore\nCharacters involved: Just Anichka, but tangentially involving anyone else spending actions in the territory\nMerits & Bonuses: \nXP Spend: \n\nProject description:Our awareness of the North Shore is generally less, so Anichka is walking the beat, getting familiar, and generally keeping an eye out for activities and flows of traffic, night events, little eddies and currents that other people may have missed. Staying undercover. Also keeping all senses open for any occult weirdness, having been told about Alice's anger issues and The Angry Woman by Ivana","project_name":"Patrolling the Shore","characters":null,"xp_spend":null,"merits":null,"bonuses":null,"detail":"Characters involved: Just Anichka, but tangentially involving anyone else spending actions in the territory\nMerits & Bonuses: \nProject description:Our awareness of the North Shore is generally less, so Anichka is walking the beat, getting familiar, and generally keeping an eye out for activities and flows of traffic, night events, little eddies and currents that other people may have missed. Staying undercover. Also keeping all senses open for any occult weirdness, having been told about Alice's anger issues and The Angry Woman by Ivana"},{"action_type":"support","action_type_raw":"Support","primary_pool":{"expression":"Wits + Occult + Cruac","size":null},"secondary_pool":null,"desired_outcome":"Assisting in ritual setup for the party that Jack and","description":"Project Name: Party Party Party\nCharacters involved: Jack, Cyrus, et al\nMerits & Bonuses: \nXP Spend: \nProject description: So there's going to be this party, and Jack would like us all to invest our time and attention. He wants to have a big ritual to help with feeding and just generally having a good one. Anichka's been put down for making feeding roles Rote (which was workshopped with Symon), so I think she adds to the ritual for that.","project_name":"Party Party Party","characters":null,"xp_spend":null,"merits":null,"bonuses":null,"detail":"Characters involved: Jack, Cyrus, et al\nMerits & Bonuses: \nProject description: So there's going to be this party, and Jack would like us all to invest our time and attention. He wants to have a big ritual to help with feeding and just generally having a good one. Anichka's been put down for making feeding roles Rote (which was workshopped with Symon), so I think she adds to the ritual for that."},{"action_type":"misc","action_type_raw":"Miscellaneous","primary_pool":{"expression":"Wits + Survival","size":null},"secondary_pool":null,"desired_outcome":"Offer a good gift to the keepers of the land","description":"Project Name: For the Others\nCharacters involved: Just Anichka\nMerits & Bonuses: \nXP Spend: \nProject description: Anichka is now aware that she's on someone else's land, or relatively close to it. She has come to the decision that she probably does not want to fight these entities, guessing them to be spirits, or locals in communion with them. She spends some time putting together a small gift for them- One of her second-tier shawls, a string of pearls, and some gathered honey from native bees (hence the Survival roll). She'll top this off with a dressing of kangaroo vine with fruit still on. Trying to position as an offering of thanks, near where she saw them last. Come back, like, twice a week to see if that's been taken or nah.","project_name":"For the Others","characters":null,"xp_spend":null,"merits":null,"bonuses":null,"detail":"Characters involved: Just Anichka\nMerits & Bonuses: \nProject description: Anichka is now aware that she's on someone else's land, or relatively close to it. She has come to the decision that she probably does not want to fight these entities, guessing them to be spirits, or locals in communion with them. She spends some time putting together a small gift for them- One of her second-tier shawls, a string of pearls, and some gathered honey from native bees (hence the Survival roll). She'll top this off with a dressing of kangaroo vine with fruit still on. Trying to position as an offering of thanks, near where she saw them last. Come back, like, twice a week to see if that's been taken or nah."}],"sphere_actions":[],"contact_actions":{"has_contacts":false,"requests":[]},"retainer_actions":{"has_retainers":true,"actions":["The family should continue living and establishing themselves, making themselves at home and part of the community, generally building their own safe space, with access to their culture for themselves and the children.\n\nIt is Orthodox Easter on the weekend of the 12th. Anichka urges her family to go if they're feeling it, especially if it will help create ties among the community and all that good shit.\n\nShe also asks them to get her a shovel, please, one for heavy duty use."]},"acquisitions":{"has_acquisitions":false,"resource_acquisitions":null,"skill_acquisitions":null},"ritual_casting":{"has_rituals":false,"casting":null},"meta":{"st_notes":"- Anichka leaves herself open to the dreams this downtime. She is concerned about the lady who is angry that Ivana has told her about, and the blood in the water that Alice has warned her about, but does not want to force herself on the issue if The Gods do not think it is important. There might be nothing of worth this dowtime, she's chill about it. Just lights some incense sometimes, dances if she feels like it, gets a lot of good nights to sleep\n- Anichka holds a little one night 'sermon' at the temple, and invites the Crone, as well as Yusuf and Charlie. My nominal concept is 'Names of the Gods;, and it's about why we do and don't need god-forces with names to worship. I'll hopefully get a wee writeup done but i'm sick as dog (as y'all know)\n- After her Animal Murder feed, she does what she can to move the bodies to where she wants her Mandragora Garden to be. Burying them if she gets the chance, but just leaving them to moulder will still help.\n- If she has the time, she will be participating in the ritual to get Cyrus back to his usual self, and shed the Crone's skin.\n- \n\n- Didn't get the chance to do a Breaking Point check for the hunt last downtime\n- In fact I'm not even sure she should be at Humanity 6, touchstone or nah.\n- I have a massive pile of things that Anichka should have had at character creation. I'm going to be trying to buy those back as quickly as possible, but sometimes that's how the cookie crumbles. So far the list includes Crafts 2, Medicine 2, Science 1 or more (botany), Academics 1 (should probably have Subterfuge too >.>), A few dots of Primal Creation, and Shed the Virulent Bowel. Probably some merits that I can't think of right now, but here's a list of things that she should have, anyway.\n\nI had more to say. I can't remember what it was. Maybe I'll open the form up again later tonight, but i'll submit this now in case I don't get that far.","xp_spend":"XP Claimed: Game Attendance 1, Costuming/Immersion 1, Downtime 1 I guess?\nTotal XP Spent:\nProject 1:\nProject 2:\nProject 3:\nProject 4:\nFree spend: Crafts 1, from shopping list.","lore_questions":null,"form_rating":8,"form_comments":null},"_character_id":"69d73ea49162ece35897a47d"},"responses":{"travel":"Same as last month, if anyone's gunna jump me then sucks to be me LOL\n\nFrom last downtime-\nShe walks, generally, or uses Obs 1 to get a late bus if she gets the chance. I know walking to and from her territory may take multiple nights, but she travels close to waterways and other places with openings to seek shelter in.","game_recount":"- Sat in a corner a lot and did handicrafts. Now all the Crone present (and Charlie) have ribbons from the hunt. Alice helped, so she'll be in any resonance from them, too.\n- Shook hands with a lot of people, especially some of the newcomers\n- Met the Bishop, that was hilarious\n- Met the Keeper's LS interest, Carver. He's interesting, and only here to learn about the past. A bit like me on that one. Mentioned the old Altar. May wanna touch base about that\n- Talked to Tegan ha ha she was not happy I dreamed about her.\n- Did what pushing I could for Alice to guard the North Shore while Charles wasn't here. I hope she gives him a run for his money on it, I think people like having someone 'innocent' in place there, we just need to make sure she gets good guidance if she stays\n- Guided plotting for next game. Made sure Jack and Cyrus (and to a lesser extent Brandi) were on it. \n- Talked to Cyrus, gave my blessing to be involved in the Hunt memories. Really wish the Keeper had been a bit more chill, he really took Cyrus's absence personally.","correspondence":"To my Sire,\n\nOh, the coven near Lviv! A very good place to remember. Are they still there? I hope they are well. I hope Halyna is well.\n\nSydney is... a tribulation. It is raw, cutting grass. A portion of ground has been cut out, but as always, our kind are hungry, circling, wanting more from a city that does not welcome us. Not yet.\n\nThere is so much to do. We have claimed two of the primary territories for feeding. This means I must walk the spaces to help keep them safe. My Maiden, Alice, has been put in charge of one. If anyone takes advantage of her, I think our Circle will take action. Probably sudden and violent action.\n\nI think there is something in the ocean, making people angry. I dreamed of an opening chest there, and our littlest says she has seen an angry lady there. We will investigate, of course, but I do not know if I should put up a wanted poster saying 'Have You Seen This Lady' or not. Time will tell.\n\nI am starting my garden. I have learned about the plants here, cut my hands on them and scratched my feet. I will make them grow and they will fruit with blood. I have also dreamed of the old temple. We will search there and find answers. But not now. We must walk the borders and let the night know what belongs to us.\n\nI wish you could see our work, but you must stay home. When I come back, Gods willing, I will show you through all I have learned.\n\nI remain in service,\nAnichka","trust":"Charlie, Alice, Ivana, with a hat tip to Jack","harm":"Nope!","aspirations":"Short term- Secure the Academy and the North Shore for the Crone, Host good party,make sure she doesn't get eaten by whoever owns the land where she lives.\nMedium term- Continued stability for the Crone, exploration and potentail restoration of the Old Temple, good Mandragora garden.\nLong term- Safety and Stability of self, family, Crone, and Praxis in that order (the middle two points are close)","rp_shoutout":"[\"Edna/Arlo\",\"we got about two minutes of tense pleasantries in but I've been waiting for it. Peter/Yusuf\",\"very strong character interactions and plotting. Good fun observing the new player in the bright orange-red suit get into character. Honourable mentions to Archer and Kurtis for solid characters that appealed to Anichka.\"]","_gate_is_regent":"no","_feed_method":"other","feeding_description":"I HEAR WE'RE HAVING A PARTY. Anichka is discerning with who she feeds from, looking for targets who haven't been drinking heavily or doing drugs (she'll branch out to 'not doing hard drugs' if finding someone with no drugs proves too hard). If it looks particularly sparse, she'll start using Auspex to try and find someone suitable, but not otherwise. Basically just trying to feed sensibly.","feeding_territories":"{\"the_academy\":\"none\",\"the_harbour\":\"none\",\"the_dockyards\":\"none\",\"the_second_city\":\"none\",\"the_north_shore\":\"none\",\"the_barrens__no_territory_\":\"none\"}","project_1_action":"patrol_scout","project_1_title":"Patrolling the Academy","project_1_outcome":"Stabilising/patrolling The Academy, and scouting weird stuff","project_1_description":"Characters involved: Just Anichka, but tangentially involving anyone else spending actions in the territory\nMerits & Bonuses: \nGenerally keeping an eye out for activities and flows of traffic, night events, little eddies and currents that other people may have missed. Staying undercover. Also keeping all senses open for any occult weirdness that Jack may have missed","project_1_pool_expr":"Wits + Stealth + Auspex","project_1_pool2_expr":"Intelligence + Occult + Auspex","project_2_action":"patrol_scout","project_2_title":"Patrolling the Shore","project_2_outcome":"Stabilising/patrolling The North Shore, and scouting weird stuff","project_2_description":"Characters involved: Just Anichka, but tangentially involving anyone else spending actions in the territory\nMerits & Bonuses: \nProject description:Our awareness of the North Shore is generally less, so Anichka is walking the beat, getting familiar, and generally keeping an eye out for activities and flows of traffic, night events, little eddies and currents that other people may have missed. Staying undercover. Also keeping all senses open for any occult weirdness, having been told about Alice's anger issues and The Angry Woman by Ivana","project_2_pool_expr":"Wits + Stealth + Auspex","project_2_pool2_expr":"Intelligence + Occult+ Auspex","project_3_action":"support","project_3_title":"Party Party Party","project_3_outcome":"Assisting in ritual setup for the party that Jack and","project_3_description":"Characters involved: Jack, Cyrus, et al\nMerits & Bonuses: \nProject description: So there's going to be this party, and Jack would like us all to invest our time and attention. He wants to have a big ritual to help with feeding and just generally having a good one. Anichka's been put down for making feeding roles Rote (which was workshopped with Symon), so I think she adds to the ritual for that.","project_3_pool_expr":"Wits + Occult + Cruac","project_4_action":"misc","project_4_title":"For the Others","project_4_outcome":"Offer a good gift to the keepers of the land","project_4_description":"Characters involved: Just Anichka\nMerits & Bonuses: \nProject description: Anichka is now aware that she's on someone else's land, or relatively close to it. She has come to the decision that she probably does not want to fight these entities, guessing them to be spirits, or locals in communion with them. She spends some time putting together a small gift for them- One of her second-tier shawls, a string of pearls, and some gathered honey from native bees (hence the Survival roll). She'll top this off with a dressing of kangaroo vine with fruit still on. Trying to position as an offering of thanks, near where she saw them last. Come back, like, twice a week to see if that's been taken or nah.","project_4_pool_expr":"Wits + Survival","retainer_1_task":"The family should continue living and establishing themselves, making themselves at home and part of the community, generally building their own safe space, with access to their culture for themselves and the children.\n\nIt is Orthodox Easter on the weekend of the 12th. Anichka urges her family to go if they're feeling it, especially if it will help create ties among the community and all that good shit.\n\nShe also asks them to get her a shovel, please, one for heavy duty use.","xp_spend":"XP Claimed: Game Attendance 1, Costuming/Immersion 1, Downtime 1 I guess?\nTotal XP Spent:\nProject 1:\nProject 2:\nProject 3:\nProject 4:\nFree spend: Crafts 1, from shopping list.","vamping":"- Anichka leaves herself open to the dreams this downtime. She is concerned about the lady who is angry that Ivana has told her about, and the blood in the water that Alice has warned her about, but does not want to force herself on the issue if The Gods do not think it is important. There might be nothing of worth this dowtime, she's chill about it. Just lights some incense sometimes, dances if she feels like it, gets a lot of good nights to sleep\n- Anichka holds a little one night 'sermon' at the temple, and invites the Crone, as well as Yusuf and Charlie. My nominal concept is 'Names of the Gods;, and it's about why we do and don't need god-forces with names to worship. I'll hopefully get a wee writeup done but i'm sick as dog (as y'all know)\n- After her Animal Murder feed, she does what she can to move the bodies to where she wants her Mandragora Garden to be. Burying them if she gets the chance, but just leaving them to moulder will still help.\n- If she has the time, she will be participating in the ritual to get Cyrus back to his usual self, and shed the Crone's skin.\n- \n\n- Didn't get the chance to do a Breaking Point check for the hunt last downtime\n- In fact I'm not even sure she should be at Humanity 6, touchstone or nah.\n- I have a massive pile of things that Anichka should have had at character creation. I'm going to be trying to buy those back as quickly as possible, but sometimes that's how the cookie crumbles. So far the list includes Crafts 2, Medicine 2, Science 1 or more (botany), Academics 1 (should probably have Subterfuge too >.>), A few dots of Primal Creation, and Shed the Virulent Bowel. Probably some merits that I can't think of right now, but here's a list of things that she should have, anyway.\n\nI had more to say. I can't remember what it was. Maybe I'll open the form up again later tonight, but i'll submit this now in case I don't get that far."},"updated_at":"2026-04-17T03:34:29.069Z","feeding_review":{"pool_player":"Undefined","pool_validated":"Wits 3 + Empathy 3 + 1 = 7","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"","pool_mod_equipment":1,"vitae_rite_cost":1,"description":"Anichka is discerning with who she feeds from, looking for targets who haven't been drinking heavily or doing drugs (she'll branch out to 'not doing hard drugs' if finding someone with no drugs proves too hard). If it looks particularly sparse, she'll start using Auspex to try and find someone suitable, but not otherwise. Basically just trying to feed sensibly.","blood_type":"Human","nine_again":false,"eight_again":false,"pool_validated_by":"Angelus","pool_committed_by":"Angelus"},"merit_actions_resolved":[{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"resolved","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"They do as they are told and she gets a very nice shovel.","created_at":"2026-04-14T09:16:15.075Z"}],"story_context":"","action_type_override":"acquisition","desired_outcome":"","description":"The family should continue living and establishing themselves, making themselves at home and part of the community, generally building their own safe space, with access to their culture for themselves and the children.\n\nIt is Orthodox Easter on the weekend of the 12th. Anichka urges her family to go if they're feeling it, especially if it will help create ties among the community and all that good shit.\n\nShe also asks them to get her a shovel, please, one for heavy duty use.","pool_resolved_by":"Angelus","merit_outcome":"approved"}],"st_review":{"territory_overrides":{"feeding":["academy"]},"travel_discretion":"subtle","outcome_text":"## Letter from Home\n\nChild,\nHalyna is well, and she is also teaching the spring rites to the younger ones in a way that would make you wince if you could see it. She learned from your notes rather than from mine, which I know because she makes the same mistake with the third invocation that you used to make, and I have chosen not to correct her because watching you both get it wrong in exactly the same way has become one of the small pleasures of my evenings.\nThe coven stands. The roof still leaks in the same corner. I mention this because you asked if they were well, and the answer is that they are exactly as they were when you left, which is the most honest measure of wellness I can offer.\nYour garden will take time. The soil in that country does not know our blood yet, and it will refuse you before it accepts you, and then it will refuse you again because it has forgotten that it already accepted you. This is not a failing on your part. It is how soil works when it has not been spoken to in eighty years. Cut your hands on it as many times as necessary. The plants do not care about your comfort; they care about your persistence.\nYou write about the angry lady in the ocean and the old temple and the borders in the same paragraph, as though they are all one problem. They are not. You know this, because you separated them in your next sentence, but I want to be clear: walk the borders first, tend the garden second, and leave the dreaming until your feet are planted somewhere solid. The old temple has waited this long and it will wait for you.\nYour Maiden Alice sounds young and recently burdened. Do not let her carry weight she has not been taught to hold. Teach her the practical things before you teach her the sacred ones, because the practical things are what will keep her standing when the sacred ones become heavy.\nI am where I have always been. The roof leaks. The coven persists. Write when you can, and write longer when you do.\n\n## Touchstone\n\nKateryna cannot sleep and has come to find you about it, carrying the blanket from her bed in a bundle against her chest as though it were something she had rescued. She stands in the doorway and announces this fact with the grave authority of a child who considers sleeplessness a serious injustice that someone ought to address.\nYou are sitting on the floor with a half-finished piece of embroidery across your knee, and you move it aside without comment to make room for her. She settles next to you, arranges the blanket into a nest around her legs, and watches your hands work the needle for a while with the particular intensity of a child who is pretending not to be tired.\nShe asks what you are making. You tell her it is a ribbon for a friend. She asks if the friend is nice, and you say yes, and she asks if the friend is here in Sydney, and you say yes, and she asks if Sydney is going to be home now, and you do not answer that one immediately because the question is larger than she knows.\nYou thread a new colour instead, a red that catches the lamplight, and she leans against your arm with the full unthinking weight of a child who has decided you are furniture. Her breathing slows. The embroidery takes shape under your hands: a pattern your grandmother taught you, carried across borders and decades and one particular kind of death, and now stitched into a ribbon in a rented house in a country where the soil does not yet know your name.\nKateryna is asleep before you finish the first repeat of the pattern. You do not move your arm.\n\n## The Barrens\n\nThe land around Ku-ring-gai does not belong to you and it does not pretend to. You have lived here for two months now and the bush has accepted your presence the way it accepts anything that does not try to change it: with indifference and the constant quiet reminder that you are a guest in something older than your kind.\nThe garden is taking root slowly, and the soil resists you exactly the way your sire said it would. You have cut your hands on the local plants often enough that you have stopped noticing the sting, and the first shoots of what you planted last month have survived, which is not the same as thriving but is enough to keep going.\nThe strange figures you glimpsed last month on the paths toward Pittwater are still there, or others like them. You catch the edges of their movement on two occasions this month: once at dusk near the fire trail above McCarrs Creek, once on the road down to Church Point. They move through the bush with a sureness that is not human and not Kindred and not animal, and they are very good at not being where you are looking by the time you look. You have decided not to follow them yet, because the land they are moving towards does not feel like it wants you to.\nThe blood this month came from the rave in the Academy rather than from the bush, which was a relief your body registered even if you did not intend to acknowledge it. Animal blood sustains, but it does not satisfy, and the difference between the two is something you are learning to carry without complaint.\n\n## Patrolling the Academy\n\nYou walk the Academy across four nights and what you come back with is the feeling more than the detail. Jack is out on the territory and you know this because the territory carries the quality of being attended to. One other patroller crosses your path near Victoria Park, a brief mutual acknowledgement and nothing more. The Beast's Hackles prickle twice on King Street where the occult shops have been busier than they should be, and once near a laneway behind Enmore Theatre where somebody has been standing for a long time without moving. You file the impressions and leave the analysis to those who patrol with more than instinct.\n\n## Patrolling the Shore\n\nThe North Shore is less familiar ground and your patrol reads it that way, in fragments rather than in the full picture. Alice is on the territory and you feel her the way you feel any Regent walking her own ground, a settled presence that tells you the territory is already watched. Brandy you catch once on Military Road, striding with the confidence of somebody who wants to be seen. The foot traffic is healthy and late and the blood would come up clean if you were feeding here. Two faces you do not place pass you near Cremorne Point, moving with the disinterest of people who are very interested in not being interesting.\n\n## Party Party Party\n\nYour part of the ritual is the oldest part and the quietest. While Cyrus holds the beat and Jack seeds the crowd and Keeper works the gantry above, you move through the room at floor level with your hands open and your Cruac running low and steady. What you are doing is not visible. It sits underneath everything else. You are weaving predatory confidence into the feeding, stitching a safety net under the bacchanal so that every Crone who reaches for blood tonight reaches with certainty. The Divination in you reads the room as it tips, each feeder's moment arriving a half-beat before they know it will, and you hold the pattern until the last of them has taken what they need. Four successes. The net holds cleanly. Nobody frenzies who should not frenzy. Nobody feeds who should not feed. Your contribution is invisible and that is exactly how you prefer it.\n\n## For the Others\n\nYou gather the honey yourself from a native bee colony in a park near the Academy, which takes the better part of a night and most of your patience. The shawl is one of your second-tier pieces, still good, still carrying the work of your hands. The pearls you add because the gesture needs weight. The kangaroo vine with fruit still on it you cut from a fence-line in Stanmore, the leaves glossy and dark. You place the offering near where you saw them last, arranged on a flat stone with the deliberateness of somebody who knows how to make an offering and who is choosing, very carefully, not to presume she knows who she is offering to. You come back twice a week across the month. The first visit, nothing has changed. The second, the honey is gone. The shawl has been moved. The pearls remain. On the third visit the vine has been replaced with a different cutting, one you did not plant, its leaves darker than any kangaroo vine you have seen in this city. Somebody has accepted the opening. Somebody has replied.\n\n## Retainer\n\nYour people do as they are told. A very nice shovel arrives by the end of the week, the handle wrapped in soft leather, the blade practical and sturdy. You will be putting it to use before long.","outcome_visibility":"published","published_at":"2026-04-17T08:16:45.334Z"},"st_narrative":{"letter_from_home":{"response":"Child,\nHalyna is well, and she is also teaching the spring rites to the younger ones in a way that would make you wince if you could see it. She learned from your notes rather than from mine, which I know because she makes the same mistake with the third invocation that you used to make, and I have chosen not to correct her because watching you both get it wrong in exactly the same way has become one of the small pleasures of my evenings.\nThe coven stands. The roof still leaks in the same corner. I mention this because you asked if they were well, and the answer is that they are exactly as they were when you left, which is the most honest measure of wellness I can offer.\nYour garden will take time. The soil in that country does not know our blood yet, and it will refuse you before it accepts you, and then it will refuse you again because it has forgotten that it already accepted you. This is not a failing on your part. It is how soil works when it has not been spoken to in eighty years. Cut your hands on it as many times as necessary. The plants do not care about your comfort; they care about your persistence.\nYou write about the angry lady in the ocean and the old temple and the borders in the same paragraph, as though they are all one problem. They are not. You know this, because you separated them in your next sentence, but I want to be clear: walk the borders first, tend the garden second, and leave the dreaming until your feet are planted somewhere solid. The old temple has waited this long and it will wait for you.\nYour Maiden Alice sounds young and recently burdened. Do not let her carry weight she has not been taught to hold. Teach her the practical things before you teach her the sacred ones, because the practical things are what will keep her standing when the sacred ones become heavy.\nI am where I have always been. The roof leaks. The coven persists. Write when you can, and write longer when you do.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete","revision_note":""},"touchstone":{"response":"Kateryna cannot sleep and has come to find you about it, carrying the blanket from her bed in a bundle against her chest as though it were something she had rescued. She stands in the doorway and announces this fact with the grave authority of a child who considers sleeplessness a serious injustice that someone ought to address.\nYou are sitting on the floor with a half-finished piece of embroidery across your knee, and you move it aside without comment to make room for her. She settles next to you, arranges the blanket into a nest around her legs, and watches your hands work the needle for a while with the particular intensity of a child who is pretending not to be tired.\nShe asks what you are making. You tell her it is a ribbon for a friend. She asks if the friend is nice, and you say yes, and she asks if the friend is here in Sydney, and you say yes, and she asks if Sydney is going to be home now, and you do not answer that one immediately because the question is larger than she knows.\nYou thread a new colour instead, a red that catches the lamplight, and she leans against your arm with the full unthinking weight of a child who has decided you are furniture. Her breathing slows. The embroidery takes shape under your hands: a pattern your grandmother taught you, carried across borders and decades and one particular kind of death, and now stitched into a ribbon in a rented house in a country where the soil does not yet know your name.\nKateryna is asleep before you finish the first repeat of the pattern. You do not move your arm.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete","revision_note":""},"territory_reports":[{"territory_id":"barrens","response":"The land around Ku-ring-gai does not belong to you and it does not pretend to. You have lived here for two months now and the bush has accepted your presence the way it accepts anything that does not try to change it: with indifference and the constant quiet reminder that you are a guest in something older than your kind.\nThe garden is taking root slowly, and the soil resists you exactly the way your sire said it would. You have cut your hands on the local plants often enough that you have stopped noticing the sting, and the first shoots of what you planted last month have survived, which is not the same as thriving but is enough to keep going.\nThe strange figures you glimpsed last month on the paths toward Pittwater are still there, or others like them. You catch the edges of their movement on two occasions this month: once at dusk near the fire trail above McCarrs Creek, once on the road down to Church Point. They move through the bush with a sureness that is not human and not Kindred and not animal, and they are very good at not being where you are looking by the time you look. You have decided not to follow them yet, because the land they are moving towards does not feel like it wants you to.\nThe blood this month came from the rave in the Academy rather than from the bush, which was a relief your body registered even if you did not intend to acknowledge it. Animal blood sustains, but it does not satisfy, and the difference between the two is something you are learning to carry without complaint.","author":"alchymiste","status":"complete","revision_note":"Seems Keeper and Carver are also possibly co-resident? This seems to be at least slightly broken, not sure it matters enough to wrry about right now."}],"action_responses":[{"action_index":0,"response":"Your people do as they are told. A very nice shovel arrives by the end of the week, the handle wrapped in soft leather, the blade practical and sturdy. You will be putting it to use before long.","author":"Von Vagabond","status":"complete","revision_note":""}],"locked":true,"project_responses":[{"project_index":0,"response":"You walk the Academy across four nights and what you come back with is the feeling more than the detail. Jack is out on the territory and you know this because the territory carries the quality of being attended to. One other patroller crosses your path near Victoria Park, a brief mutual acknowledgement and nothing more. The Beast's Hackles prickle twice on King Street where the occult shops have been busier than they should be, and once near a laneway behind Enmore Theatre where somebody has been standing for a long time without moving. You file the impressions and leave the analysis to those who patrol with more than instinct.","author":"Von Vagabond","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":1,"response":"The North Shore is less familiar ground and your patrol reads it that way, in fragments rather than in the full picture. Alice is on the territory and you feel her the way you feel any Regent walking her own ground, a settled presence that tells you the territory is already watched. Brandy you catch once on Military Road, striding with the confidence of somebody who wants to be seen. The foot traffic is healthy and late and the blood would come up clean if you were feeding here. Two faces you do not place pass you near Cremorne Point, moving with the disinterest of people who are very interested in not being interesting.","author":"Von Vagabond","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":2,"response":"Your part of the ritual is the oldest part and the quietest. While Cyrus holds the beat and Jack seeds the crowd and Keeper works the gantry above, you move through the room at floor level with your hands open and your Cruac running low and steady. What you are doing is not visible. It sits underneath everything else. You are weaving predatory confidence into the feeding, stitching a safety net under the bacchanal so that every Crone who reaches for blood tonight reaches with certainty. The Divination in you reads the room as it tips, each feeder's moment arriving a half-beat before they know it will, and you hold the pattern until the last of them has taken what they need. Four successes. The net holds cleanly. Nobody frenzies who should not frenzy. Nobody feeds who should not feed. Your contribution is invisible and that is exactly how you prefer it.","author":"Von Vagabond","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":3,"response":"You gather the honey yourself from a native bee colony in a park near the Academy, which takes the better part of a night and most of your patience. The shawl is one of your second-tier pieces, still good, still carrying the work of your hands. The pearls you add because the gesture needs weight. The kangaroo vine with fruit still on it you cut from a fence-line in Stanmore, the leaves glossy and dark. You place the offering near where you saw them last, arranged on a flat stone with the deliberateness of somebody who knows how to make an offering and who is choosing, very carefully, not to presume she knows who she is offering to. You come back twice a week across the month. The first visit, nothing has changed. The second, the honey is gone. The shawl has been moved. The pearls remain. On the third visit the vine has been replaced with a different cutting, one you did not plant, its leaves darker than any kangaroo vine you have seen in this city. Somebody has accepted the opening. Somebody has replied.","author":"Von Vagabond","status":"complete","revision_note":""}]},"projects_resolved":[{"action_type":"patrol_scout","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[7,4,1,2,1,1,8]","successes":1,"exceptional":false,"rolled_at":"2026-04-17T03:44:06.963Z","params":{"size":7,"again":10,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"Wits + Stealth + Auspex","pool_validated":"Wits 3 + Stealth 2 + Auspex 2 = 7","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"active_feed_specs":[],"pool_mod_spec":0,"nine_again":false,"rote":false,"eight_again":false,"pool_committed_by":"Angelus","pool_validated_by":"Angelus"},{"action_type":"patrol_scout","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[5,4,6,7,9,0>1,6]","successes":2,"exceptional":false,"rolled_at":"2026-04-17T03:43:59.769Z","params":{"size":7,"again":10,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"Wits + Stealth + Auspex","pool_validated":"Wits 3 + Stealth 2 + Auspex 2 = 7","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"active_feed_specs":[],"pool_mod_spec":0,"nine_again":false,"rote":false,"eight_again":false,"pool_committed_by":"Angelus","pool_validated_by":"Angelus"},{"action_type":"support","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[2,8,3,5,3,7,8,0>6,0>3,2]","successes":4,"exceptional":false,"rolled_at":"2026-04-17T03:44:29.557Z","params":{"size":10,"again":10,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"Wits + Occult + Cruac","pool_validated":"Wits 3 + Occult 4 + Cruac 3 = 10","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"active_feed_specs":[],"pool_mod_spec":0,"nine_again":false,"rote":false,"eight_again":false,"pool_committed_by":"Angelus","pool_validated_by":"Angelus"},{"action_type":"misc","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[1,8,4,4,3,2]","successes":1,"exceptional":false,"rolled_at":"2026-04-17T03:45:27.490Z","params":{"size":6,"again":10,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"Wits + Survival","pool_validated":"Wits 3 + Survival 3 = 6","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"The things she is seeing are Changelings. She does not know this (the player suspects).","resolved_at":null,"active_feed_specs":[],"pool_mod_spec":0,"nine_again":false,"rote":false,"eight_again":false,"pool_committed_by":"Angelus","title":"For the Others","desired_outcome":"Offer a good gift to the keepers of the land","description":"Anichka is now aware that she's on someone else's land, or relatively close to it. She has come to the decision that she probably does not want to fight these entities, guessing them to be spirits, or locals in communion with them. She spends some time putting together a small gift for them- One of her second-tier shawls, a string of pearls, and some gathered honey from native bees (hence the Survival roll). She'll top this off with a dressing of kangaroo vine with fruit still on. Trying to position as an offering of thanks, near where she saw them last. Come back, like, twice a week to see if that's been taken or nah.","merits_bonuses":"","pool_validated_by":"Angelus"}],"feeding_vitae_tally":{"herd":2,"ambience":2,"ambience_territory":"Academy","oath_of_fealty":0,"ghouls":0,"rite_cost":1,"manual":0,"total_bonus":3},"feeding_roll_player":{"cols":[{"r":{"v":10,"s":true,"x":true},"ch":[{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false}]},{"r":{"v":1,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":3,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":9,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":3,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":4,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":7,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]}],"successes":3,"vessels":3,"safeVitae":6,"methodName":"Other","pool":7,"again":10,"breakdown":"ST confirmed: Wits 3 + Empathy 3 + 1 = 7","rolledAt":"2026-04-17T09:39:16.033Z","dramaticFailure":false},"feeding_vitae_allocation":[2,2,2]}];
