1-/**
2: * crd.3a — real behavioural coverage for the server-side resolve endpoint
3: * (Epic CRD, specs/stories/crd-3a-server-resolve-endpoint.md).
4- *
5: *   AC1 — PUT /:id/resolve exists, reuses _findChallenge (404/409), and
6- *         requires target-character ownership (403), mirroring accept/decline.
7- *   AC2 — computes the base pool as the EFFECTIVE (dots + bonus) value of the
8- *         Resistance Attribute matching defender_aspect, read fresh from the
9- *         defender's LIVE character document.
10- *   AC3/AC9 — a true defender_wp_spent re-checks CURRENT live Willpower
11- *         (tracker_state, never cached/submitted), 409s at <= 0, else +2 (not
12- *         +3); only a strict boolean true triggers a spend.
13- *   AC4/AC5 — defender_merit_ids validated against the character's REAL
14- *         merits[] on rule_key; an unowned id is silently dropped; only
15- *         Indomitable (+2 flat) and Closed Book (+rating) contribute — any
16- *         other owned merit contributes 0 but is not dropped.
17: *   AC6/AC7 — writes defender_pool/aspect/wp_spent/merit_ids, status stays
18- *         'pending', and re-resolving fully recomputes and overwrites.
19: *   AC8 — the crd.1 accept-route guard still 409s an unresolved challenge,
20: *         and accepts normally once resolved through this endpoint.
21- *
22- * Follows crd-1-contested-roll-request-shape.test.js's exact fixture/cleanup/
23- * describe.skipIf(!dbAvailable) shape. No browser, no Playwright — this
24- * story has no client-visible surface.
25- *
26- * DB-backed: real MongoDB required. See db-setup.js.
27- */
